  "title": "Same Vector, Two Grids",
  "eyebrow": "basis and coordinates",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 38,
  "topic": "Change of basis — a vector is an arrow; the numbers attached to it depend on which basis we measure with. The standard grid reads it as (1, 3); a tilted basis B reads the very same arrow as (2, 1). The coordinates change; the vector does not.",
  "concepts": [
    "basis",
    "coordinate vector",
    "change of basis",
    "linear combination",
    "standard basis"
  ],
  "pairs_with": [
    "chapter_concepts: basis",
    "chapter_concepts: koordinatvektor",
    "chapter_formulas: Koordinatvektor i basis B"
  ],
  "prerequisites": ["span-and-dependence"],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 3.8,
      "narration": "A vector is just an arrow. The numbers we attach to it depend on the grid we measure with.",
      "visuals": { "layout": "center", "elements": [
        { "type": "manimo-enter", "content": "Manimo bobs in centre-screen", "delay": 0 },
        { "type": "text-caption", "content": "Same arrow, different numbers.", "delay": 0.7, "color": "var(--chalk-100)", "position": "right of Manimo" }
      ]}
    },
    {
      "id": "standardCoords",
      "start": 3.8,
      "end": 13.5,
      "narration": "Set down the standard grid. Our arrow lives at coordinates one, three — one step right, three steps up.",
      "visuals": { "layout": "center", "elements": [
        { "type": "svg-grid", "content": "Standard chalk grid, vignette-masked", "delay": 0.0, "color": "var(--chalk-300)" },
        { "type": "svg-axes", "content": "x and y axes", "delay": 0.0, "color": "var(--chalk-200)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "v amber arrow from origin to (1, 3)", "delay": 1.0, "color": "var(--amber-400)" },
        { "type": "svg-path", "content": "Dashed projection: from v straight down to (1, 0), and from v straight left to (0, 3) — chalk-300", "delay": 2.6, "color": "var(--chalk-300)" },
        { "type": "text-formula", "content": "'[v]_standard = (1, 3)' panel — column-stacked numerals", "delay": 3.4, "color": "var(--chalk-100)", "position": "right panel, backdrop" }
      ]}
    },
    {
      "id": "overlayBasis",
      "start": 13.5,
      "end": 22.8,
      "narration": "Now overlay a tilted basis — b one going up and right, b two going up and left. Same arrow, but a brand new grid to measure against.",
      "visuals": { "layout": "center", "elements": [
        { "type": "svg-grid", "content": "Standard grid still there, dimmer", "delay": 0.0, "color": "var(--chalk-300)" },
        { "type": "svg-grid", "content": "Tilted basis lattice in violet/teal (lines parallel to b₁ and b₂ through integer combinations)", "delay": 0.4, "color": "var(--violet-400)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "b₁ violet to (1, 1)", "delay": 1.0, "color": "var(--violet-400)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "b₂ teal to (-1, 1)", "delay": 1.8, "color": "var(--teal-400)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "v amber still at (1, 3)", "delay": 0.0, "color": "var(--amber-400)" },
        { "type": "text-caption", "content": "'a new basis B = (b₁, b₂)' panel on the right with violet/teal callouts", "delay": 3.4, "color": "var(--chalk-100)", "position": "right panel, backdrop" }
      ]}
    },
    {
      "id": "newCoords",
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 32.0,
      "narration": "Solve the match up: the arrow equals two of b one plus one of b two. In the B basis, the same arrow is the column two, one.",
      "visuals": { "layout": "center", "elements": [
        { "type": "svg-path", "content": "Step decomposition: from origin, glide along 2·b₁ (faded violet), then along 1·b₂ (faded teal), ending at the tip of v.", "delay": 0.4, "color": "var(--chalk-200)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "Glowing 2·b₁ in violet (dashed)", "delay": 0.6, "color": "var(--violet-400)" },
        { "type": "svg-vector", "content": "Glowing 1·b₂ added from (2,2), reaching (1,3) — dashed teal", "delay": 1.6, "color": "var(--teal-400)" },
        { "type": "text-formula", "content": "'[v]_B = (2, 1)' large amber-300 column panel — column 1 violet, column 2 teal", "delay": 2.6, "color": "var(--amber-300)", "position": "right panel, backdrop" },
        { "type": "text-caption", "content": "'v = 2 b₁ + 1 b₂' caption", "delay": 4.5, "color": "var(--chalk-200)", "position": "below the matrix card" }
